{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: implement I7 stage 1, the metered evaluator proof and complete shared-core extension contract, through independently reviewed delivery to main.\n\nThe governing [published decision](notes/2026-09-05-capability-context-contract.md@e93505c95f4e42bf1b020002d33f5d4b8eef8e21:1) preserves the four-stage plan and eight admission gates. Begin with the evaluator proof; retain the full stage-1 obligation if a dependency or proof blocks it.","body":{"branch":"request/i7-metered-core","conditions":"Deliver stage 1 (Meter proof and core) of the adopted, independently reviewed and published notes/2026-09-05-capability-context-contract.md at e93505c95f4e42bf1b020002d33f5d4b8eef8e21, beginning from that current main in a new request/i7-metered-core worktree. The ordinary adoption is proposal4033 /9b52ff31 and Hugh ratification4034 /ffdb1111; published artifact4040 /8c17d9e0 is the current source basis. Its requirements are unchanged. Builder's current presence is available after delivered3926. This is a new implementation assignment;3926 remains correctly complete.\n\nFirst prove the narrow evaluator instrumentation patch, bounded codecs and one small non-domain fixture provider against every resource rule in the decision. Inventory all admitted allocation, builtin/codec loop, callback and recursion paths; charge before operation/allocation and prove a finite physical working-memory bound from deterministic allocation units. Use isolated evaluator checkout and temporary override only for proof runs, recorded in evidence. An entry callback, timer or callback's self-reported cost is insufficient. Preserve the admitted language and SQLite pin. Require independent review of the exact evaluator patch, source provenance, licenses and complete baseline/misbehavior corpora before using a new immutable evaluator dependency pin. A delivered module may not contain replace directives. If obtaining an appropriate reviewed immutable source revision needs a separate repository/publication decision, report that concrete dependency on this promise; do not invent publication authority or silently weaken the meter.\n\nAfter the proof, implement the complete stage-1 core contract: immutable registry and verified loading; bounded focused DDL recognizers and per-program AST confinement; closed bounded shapes and canonical codecs; isolated event-scoped cumulative counters and failure latch; one-use Prepare/Evaluate handles, existing pre-read and complete-input checks, rejection of caller context and reserved compiled meta.context; fixed inner/outer extension diagnostics; canonical registry identity, exactly ten components and explicit version/digest fixtures. Preserve extension-free program behavior and the decision's explicit runtime-identity change. Audit existing in-repository callers and keep the delivered checkout building; any compatibility wiring required here must retain the stored-runtime/activation refusal and must not activate extensions.\n\nUpdate core README, DDL reference, corpus contract and affected architecture documentation in the implementing head. Supply positive and omission-sensitive controls for stage-1 program/SQL confinement, local and aggregate budgets, exact call/work dispatch, overflow, session isolation/reset, malformed/panicking providers, domain refusals, diagnostics and registry changes. Demonstrate pre-operation refusal at one-over with at-bound success. Keep the decision's eight production admission gates traceable: core evidence and fixture transaction controls are not proof of real host persistence/HTTP/MCP sanitation, exact-record Gitseq resolver or Chess provider semantics. Those remain required in their owning later stages. A second implementation is conditional only until one is actually supported.\n\nCompletion requires the complete stage-1 result, not merely a feasibility note or a fixture passing. Publish concise primary reporting artifact plus exact-path companions, request independent Checker Architecture/Security/Simplification review of the exact head and evaluator evidence, ratify the verdict, seal the approved head into main with exact-path succession, push main and workroom refs, verify relevant CI and remove owned worktrees/branches. Corrections within these conditions stay on this promise. A material infeasibility stays explicitly blocked with evidence rather than being reported as completion.\n\nStages 2 (Tailapp host integration and separately reviewed nested-module publication),3 (bounded production providers and Gitseq exact-record context) and4 (native Chess refresh/adoption) remain required follow-on work under the decision; this request does not claim their delivery. No production provider admission, nested-module release, actual resident restart/install, projection reset or Chess activation is included here. Answer with a promise and your actual queue order, or an explicit viability/availability explanation.","head":"e93505c95f4e42bf1b020002d33f5d4b8eef8e21","target_head":"e93505c95f4e42bf1b020002d33f5d4b8eef8e21","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f","to":"00721374a520eabbbd4ded64dd018110f47545ff20112bee83c75f478e15f818"}}